{
  "name": "root",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "license": "ISC",
  "scripts": {
    "bench": "tsx ./scripts/bench.ts",
    "examples": "tsx ./scripts/examples.ts",
    "release": "pnpm -F koota build && pnpm -F koota test run && pnpm -F koota publish",
    "prepublishOnly": "pnpm -F koota build && pnpm -F koota generate-tests",
    "test": "pnpm -F core test run && pnpm -F react test run",
    "test:build": "pnpm prepublishOnly && pnpm -F koota test run",
    "lint": "pnpm -r lint",
    "format": "prettier --config .config/prettier/base.json --write ."
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@clack/prompts": "^1.0.1",
    "@types/node": "^24.10.1",
    "oxlint": "^1.36.0",
    "prettier": "latest",
    "tsx": "latest",
    "typescript": "latest"
  },
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=24.2.0",
    "pnpm": ">=10.12.1"
  },
  "packageManager": "pnpm@10.28.1"
}packages:
  - packages/*
  - examples/*
  - examples/tools/*
  - benches/*
  - .config/*

catalog:
  '@react-three/drei': ^10.7.7
  '@react-three/fiber': ^9.4.0
  '@types/react': ^19.2.6
  '@types/react-dom': ^19.2.3
  '@types/three': ^0.181.0
  directed: ^0.1.6
  "mitata": "^1.0.34"
  react: ^19.2.0
  react-dom: ^19.2.0
  three: ^0.181.2
  unplugin-inline-functions: ^0.3.10
  vite: ^7.2.4
  vitest: ^4.0.13

manage-package-manager-versions: true

onlyBuiltDependencies:
  - '@swc/core'
  - esbuild
This monorepo uses `pnpm`.

**IMPORTANT:** Always use kebab-case for file names, even if it is not the usual convention.

The `skills/koota` directory contains a skill with reference documentation for the koota project. When updating the README, the skill should be updated as well to keep documentation in sync. Follow best practices for agent skills.

## Benchmarks

Benchmarks live in `benches/`. Each benchmark is a directory with a `src/main.ts` entry point.

```sh
# Interactive GUI selector
pnpm bench

# Run one or more suites by name (partial match works)
pnpm bench <name> [name2 ...]

# Comma-separated names also work
pnpm bench <name1,name2,...>

# Replay last selection without prompting
pnpm bench --last
```
